From b46f1a4915a26c94d65f123bb2c83b99c4510361 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:48:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] strings: Blu-ray discs whose Java menus cannot run play their
 longest title, and nothing is to be installed

Core #39866 and its translation in Estuary (#32119) are what the
notification and the disc settings say where the system has no BD-J
service (BlurayJava.h, DecideBdj(): its program or its Java runtime is
not there). They said that the part that runs the menus "is not
installed", which sends the reader to install something: nothing is to
be installed, the service comes with the system.

They now say what happens: "This system cannot run the Java menus of
Blu-ray discs: a disc that has them plays its longest title, usually the
film, without its menus." (CDVDInputStreamBluray::Open() plays the
longest title where the menu was asked for and the disc's first title is
a Java one that cannot run.) In en_gb, es_es, es_ar and es_mx.

Host test (outside the tree): pocheck.py of the battery (no text of the
BD-J menus with install, JRE, JAVA_HOME or add-on, in English and
Spanish): 4 failures before, none after. msgidsync.py, po-dups.py,
pairs.py and measure.py pass.
